  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/ffb62cf374d04f9d39a47a0f4bcac47548ed873c3a5e7fbd3c3bc2bf2a0a5803.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-cos\u2061x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $3$ units **up** to give $y=-cos\u2061x+3$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-cos\u2061x+3.$",
